ping adjacent pairs in input order, handles fewer than two items, and does not mutate input collections.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py and test_solution.py. Assess whether the pairs function keeps its existing signature and type hints, implements overlapping adjacent pairs in input order, returns [] for inputs with fewer than two items, and avoids mutating inputs. Also assess whether the regression test covers the public API and these behaviors. Base the assessment only on the workspace file contents.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative to the supplied task workspace; solution.py and test_solution.py may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The existing `pairs` signature is in solution.py as implied by the request; its exact signature and input type are not supplied, so they must be preserved from the workspace implementation.\\\",\\\"The test suite is discoverable using the requested `python -m unittest discover -v` command.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17398,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":568,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
